    "media:imagetext": "100 BE B\nHISTORIC PLANES OF TRANS WORLD AIRLINES\nTHE\nCARO\nBICENTENNIAL\nUSA\nTRI MOTOR\nTWA\nANNIVERSARY\nThe Ford Tri-motor \"City\nThe Tri-motor was the\nJuxury aircraft of its day\nVentilation (the windows\ncould be opened), heating\nand courier service were new.\nTWA\nThe mail contracts allowed the airlines to survive during\nThe\nthe lean years of the Depression\nTri-motors were retired from passenger service in 1954\n-and converted to haul freight in 1936\nThe original\nFlying Boxcars\"",
